# DRY and SOLID

Mandatory reference before any new feature, refactor, or code review.

**Write all docs and rules in English** (see `.cursor/rules/language.mdc`).

## DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)

| Layer | Single source | Do not duplicate |
|-------|---------------|------------------|
| Frontend HTTP | `packages/api-client` (`apiFetch`, `auth.ts`, `getApiErrorMessage`) | `fetch` in `apps/*` |
| Intuit / QBO | `backend/app/Services/QuickBooksService.php` | QBO SDK outside the service |
| QBO rate limits | `.cursor/rules/quickbooks-api.mdc` (cache, `FindById`, manual refresh) | Uncached list endpoints, redundant SDK calls |
| UI errors (EN) | `getApiErrorMessage()` + API `error` codes | Raw backend messages in apps |
| Session auth | `apiFetch` (CSRF + cookies) | Per-app Sanctum logic |
| Prod config | `.env.example` + README Production | Magic values in code |

**Before adding a function or component:** search for existing code (`grep`, `@ellr/api-client`, `QuickBooksService`). If logic appears twice, extract at the right level (api-client, Laravel service, or shared helper).

**Acceptable exceptions:** very simple local UI (login form) as long as it stays thin with no duplicated business logic.

## SOLID (applied to the monorepo)

| Principle | Concrete rule |
|-----------|----------------|
| **S** Single Responsibility | Controllers: validation + JSON orchestration. Services: business + QBO. React apps: render + UI state. |
| **O** Open/Closed | Extend via services/config, not by editing `QuickBooksService` for an isolated UI case. |
| **L** Liskov | Respect public contracts (`apiFetch`, JSON responses documented in README). |
| **I** Interface Segregation | Minimal exports in `packages/api-client/src/index.ts`. No catch-all API. |
| **D** Dependency Inversion | Backend: inject `QuickBooksService` in controllers. Frontend: depend on `@ellr/api-client`, not hardcoded API URLs. |

## Red flags (fix or reject in review)

- Second HTTP client, second QBO error mapping, second OAuth flow.
- Business logic (QBO employee, tokens, validation) in a controller or `App.tsx`.
- Copy-paste of > 10 lines between admin and timesheet without extraction.
- New endpoint without a Pest test; `api-client` change without `api.test.ts`.

## Agent routine (every task)

1. Identify the layer (api-client / `@ellr/ui` / backend service / app UI).
2. Check that an abstraction already exists; extend it rather than duplicate.
3. Keep controllers and `App.tsx` thin; extract when past soft limits (see `.cursor/rules/file-structure.mdc`).
4. Update tests + rules if a new pattern becomes the project norm.
5. Read the detailed plan: `docs/dry-reusability-plan.md` before any new UI feature or QBO endpoint.

## File size (pragmatic SRP)

See `.cursor/rules/file-structure.mdc` for targets. Summary: `App.tsx` ≤ ~80 lines (composition root), feature hooks in `hooks/`, screen sections in `components/`, Laravel controllers thin, services ≤ ~250 lines unless splitting a real domain boundary.

## Reusability roadmap (summary)

| Phase | Content | Priority |
|-------|---------|----------|
| 1 | `quickbooks.ts` + `timesheet.ts` in api-client | P0 |
| 2 | `@ellr/ui` package (useAuth, LoginForm, Alert, AppShell) | P0 |
| 3 | `@ellr/test-utils` (mocks, login fixtures) | P1 |
| 4 | `TimeActivityService` + Form Requests + `QuickBooksTokenResolverService` | P0 backend |
| 5 | Shared Vite/Vitest config | P2 |

Do not add duplicated logic in admin/timesheet while waiting for the relevant phase; prefer api-client or a Laravel service.
